  "note": "Found in the notes profile with column breaks (seed 19, document 99). Reduced form: an A6 page with a view of two auto-fill columns in three segments: segment 0 (a 14 pt text with lineHeight 2, an 8 pt text of two lines, a view 12 pt high, and a 14 pt text of four lines with break=\"column\"), a span text, and segment 2, a 14 pt text of 13 tokens (seven lines of two words). Column 1 of segment 0 is 28 + 19.2 + 12 = 59.2 pt, column 2 is 4 x 16.8 = 67.2 pt, so the filled row is 67.2 pt high and the stacked galley 126.4 pt. Segment 0 ends on page 2, so pagination keeps its filled row (split-stack.ts:288-293, `withFilledRows`) and splits segment 2 at its top from the stacked layout (split-stack.ts:137, `topOf(child)`), 59.2 pt too low. Segment 2 has 120.4 pt above the notes; the split sees 120.4 - 59.2 = 61.2 pt, so its columns end at three lines (47.1 pt), where four lines (62.5 pt) would hold all seven lines and bring no note. Without the break it passes. Not fixed.",
